ield); used of a serpent (as coiling itself), probably the \"asp\"","p":null,"t":"aspis","g":"of vipers","fb":[],"v":[28002]},"G765":{"l":"ἀσεβής","x":"asebḗs","d":"irreverent, i.e. (by extension) impious or wicked","p":null,"t":"asebes","g":"ungodly","fb":[],"v":[28025,28051,29699,30458,30499,30500,30523,30671,30682,30682]},"G771":{"l":"ἀσθένημα","x":"asthénēma","d":"a scruple of conscience","p":null,"t":"asthenema","g":"weaknesses","fb":[],"v":[28302]},"G711":{"l":"Ἀριστόβουλος","x":"Aristóboulos","d":"best counselling; Aristoboulus, a Christian","p":null,"t":"aristoboulos","g":"of Aristobulus","fb":[["aristobulus","Aristobulus","Man living at the time of the New Testament","Paul greets his household and not the man himself, who may have died or may not have believed. Some think he was a grandson of Herod the Great known from Josephus to have lived in Rome, but that cannot be confirmed.","person",1]],"v":[28344]},"G799":{"l":"Ἀσύγκριτος","x":"Asýnkritos","d":"incomparable; Asyncritus, a Christian","p":null,"t":"asynkritos","g":"Asyncritus","fb":[["asyncritos","Asyncritos","Man living at the time of the New Testament","Greeted by Paul with Phlegon, Hermas, Patrobas, Hermes and others in Rome. Beyond his name and that group nothing is known.","person",1]],"v":[28348]},"G753":{"l":"ἀρχιτέκτων","x":"architéktōn","d":"a chief constructor, i.e. \"architect\"","p":null,"t":"architekton","g":"master builder","fb":[],"v":[28415]},"G790":{"l":"ἀστατέω","x":"astatéō","d":"to be non-stationary, i.e. (figuratively) homeless","p":null,"t":"astateo","g":"wander homeless","fb":[],"v":[28439]},"G733":{"l":"ἀρσενοκοίτης","x":"arsenokoítēs","d":"a sodomite","p":null,"t":"arsenokoites","g":"homosexuals","fb":[],"v":[28471,29700]},"G728":{"l":"ἀῤῥαβών","x":"arrhabṓn","d":"a pledge, i.e. part of the purchase-money or property given in advance as security for the rest","p":null,"t":"arrhabon","g":"pledge","fb":[],"v":[28817,28877,29214]},"G718":{"l":"ἁρμόζω","x":"harmózō","d":"to joint,